{"id": "DeHWj2lT1Rb", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does Maa Kalaratri, the SCARIEST form of Durga, ride a DONKEY? 🫏 The answer is so beautiful 👇\n\nKalaratri is Maa Durga’s 7th form, worshipped on Navratri Day 7. KAAL means dark, RATRI means night: skin darker than the night, wild open hair, a third eye, breath of fire, a necklace of lightning and a garland of skulls.\n\nWhy so fierce? She came to defeat Raktabija, the demon whose every drop of blood became another demon. Not one drop touched the ground.\n\nAnd her ride? A horse runs from a wolf. A donkey doesn’t. Farmers still keep donkeys to guard their sheep. The goddess who destroys fear rides the one animal that won’t run, and the humblest one.\n\nHer other name is SHUBHANKARI, the one who brings only good. Scary to demons, gentle to her children. 🙏\n\n📚 Book 7, Kalaratri: The Fierce Dark Knight, is coming soon!\nBooks 1–3 of our Navadurga picture-book series are out now: set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\nIs your name Kali, Kalika, Shyama or Shubha? Comment your name! Or tag someone who has one 👇\nSave this for Navratri Day 7 and share it with a little one who’s scared of the dark 🌙\n\n#Navratri #Navratri2026 #Kalaratri #MaaKalaratri #NavratriDay7 Navadurga MaaDurga Durga Saptami HinduMythology IndianMythology KidsBooks PictureBooks StoriesForKids RishiKatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1791208169, "like_count": 13573, "comment_count": 53, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1385218247029337a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 50.434, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMsRxwZOsSqZQy9aVqTDtsamBi3b6B9Kyl31vErqWLsxUc16sTpY_XPUKb5QznPbXqu6Lh3om7iOd3MnBMdfRC7y8NhNHhW_S9YMZI.mp4?_nc_cat=101&_nc_oc=AdqsRpmD8amDNm-CyrptJVtfPgj